pped by the translation — no missing module to translate.\n- **ERRORS.md** — grepping for every rejection mechanism returned **zero** hits (no `return`, `assert`, `NULL`, `errno`, `enum`, range check, or even a single `if`). With a `void` return and two by-value `int`s there is no error channel and no invalid input. I filled the 16 rows with the failure conditions the code *can* face (stdout write failures) and every domain boundary, including out-of-`int`-range bit patterns.\n- **CONFIGS.md** — 26 rows across four derived axes; `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` table**, so there is exactly one feature combination.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **`putchar` vs `puts`** — the `release` cdylib imports `putchar` because LLVM rewrites `puts(\"\")` → `putchar('\\n')`. My first symbol test used a hand-written libc allowlist and flagged this as a failure. It's a false positive (GCC does the same at `-O2`, bytes are identical), so I replaced the allowlist with `ldd -r`, which asks the dynamic linker itself. I verified byte-equality for the release artifact including under `setvbuf(_IONBF)`, where each call reaches `write(2)` separately.\n2. **Two test-harness bugs I found and fixed in my own tooling** — `cargo test` does not build a `cdylib`, and it stops at the first failing test *target*. Without `--no-fail-fast` my mutation tallies silently covered only Phase B (25 of 46 tests). Both fixed; tallies now sum to 46.\n\n## Negative control (`./mutation_check.sh`)\n\nSince everything passed on the first run, I verified the suite can fail. Six wrong variants injected, original always restored:\n\n| mutant | caught / survived |\n|---|---|\n| `x \\| y`, `x & !y`, `!x \\| y`, `y \\| !x` | 41 / 5 |\n| `x ^ !y` | 35 / 11 |\n| `(x \\| !y) + 1` | 43 / 0 arithmetic |\n\nEvery mutant detected, with the first divergent input localized. Each survivor is *provably* insensitive rather than a gap — row 10 pins `x = -1` (both forms give `-1`), row 12 pins `x == y`, rows 11/17/26 pin `y = -1`.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- ☑ Symbol diff empty, `ldd -r` reports 0 unresolved (debug **and** release)\n- ☑ 26/26 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass — >1.1M randomized/exhaustive inputs, fixed seed\n- ☑ 16/16 `ERRORS.md` rows pass, with assertions that each injected failure was non-vacuous\n- ☑ All of it under every feature combination (1) **plus** the release profile\n\n`cargo test` never links the crate directly — it's `cdylib`-only, so all 41 call sites go through `dlopen`/`dlsym`, exercising the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper as an external caller would. `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the `build/` directory the task's own instructions create.","ttft_ms":17194,"ttft_stream_ms":17021,"time_to_request_ms":35,"type":"result","duration_ms":1365294,"uuid":"670053e8-afc1-46c2-87eb-415321d672de"}
